WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:09.350
On a jobsite, hazards get found all day. The hard part is proving every one got fixed. Here's how Safely Track closes that loop for general contractors.

00:00:10.317 --> 00:00:24.317
It starts on the phone. A superintendent snaps a photo, and AI drafts the observation: the hazard, the risk, and the OSHA 1926 standard. They check it, and pick the sub who owns the fix.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:33.300
The corrective action goes to that subcontractor's foreman by text, with a link. No login, no app, and no training for their crews.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:39.400
The foreman opens the link on their phone, adds a photo of the fix, and marks it done.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:47.850
And it's on the record: who found it, who fixed it, and how long it took. This one closed in two hours.

00:00:48.783 --> 00:00:55.033
Across every project, you see what's still open, what's overdue, and which trade it's waiting on.

00:00:55.983 --> 00:01:03.683
Site audits run on your own forms, organized by 1926 subpart, with every trade on site and every finding cited.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:12.800
Toolbox talks go out as a QR code for each project. Sub crews sign in on their own phones, and the sign-in sheet builds itself.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:22.350
When something does happen, the incident, its root cause, and the corrective action live in one place, and recordables flow straight to your OSHA 300 log.

00:01:23.317 --> 00:01:31.667
And leadership sees the trend: findings against OSHA's ten most-cited standards, repeat citations, and how fast each issue gets closed.

00:01:32.617 --> 00:01:39.217
Bring a real report from one of your jobs. We'll run it through Safely Track live, in thirty minutes.
